      "content": "i get that it's just chemistry, but it's just so frustrating. it feels like the more i try to stabilize it, the more it reacts. it's like the battery is actively resisting being contained, almost like it's being spiteful or trying to sabotage my work. i've seen tech videos where people talk about these 'rogue' cells that behave totally differently from the manual. is there any reason it would seem like it's intentionally acting out or being difficult on purpose?",
